    {
      "text": "The `close` method belongs to the `HTTPAdapter` class in the requests library and is responsible for releasing the resources the adapter holds onto.",
      "type": "intent",
      "subtype": "purpose",
      "slots": {}
    },
    {
      "text": "Its docstring explains the intent: it shuts down the adapter's connection pooling machinery so that any open sockets tied to pooled connections get cleaned up.",
      "type": "intent",
      "subtype": "purpose",
      "slots": {}
    },
    {
      "text": "The first step calls `clear()` on `self.poolmanager`, which is a urllib3 `PoolManager` that caches connection pools keyed by host and scheme; clearing it closes the pools and the connections inside them.",
